      }
    },
    "386": {
      "date": "2026-10-16",
      "edition": "Friday 16 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Coaching scrutiny",
          "heading": "Andy Goode calls England's failure to talk to Shaun Edwards 'mind boggling'",
          "body": "Former England fly-half Andy Goode says no meaningful talks were held with Shaun Edwards, who has instead taken a coaching role with Argentina, and calls the omission 'mind boggling'. England, who have lost five of eight matches this year and conceded 29 tries, need England head coach Steve Borthwick to give attack coach Lee Blackett full licence, Goode argues. \"It's mind boggling why you wouldn't at least have the conversation,\" he says, and he believes the RFU has blundered."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
