    "387": {
      "date": "2026-10-16",
      "edition": "Friday 16 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Power debate",
          "heading": "James A Lucas warns France's success could crush rugby like cricket",
          "body": "Kick Off columnist James A Lucas argues France's success is itself the threat to rugby, dismissing the idea that the French are villains and saying their intentions are irrelevant. Lucas recalls a social-media plea asking the rugby gods not to let France kill the sport as India killed cricket, which drew puzzled, offended responses from France and its defenders. The sport would be poorer without France, those defenders countered, pointing to the number of players France employs and its profitable league."
        },
