      "edition": "Friday 16 October",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Champions Cup",
          "heading": "Leinster and Munster lead four Irish provinces into Champions Cup this weekend",
          "body": "The four Irish provinces open their Champions Cup campaigns this weekend, the competition's first October start since 2018, after only three league games. Leinster, beaten 41-19 by Bordeaux-Bègles in May's final, have not won the trophy since 2018, while Munster dropped into the Challenge Cup last season after losing at home to Castres in their final pool game. Munster have not secured a home knockout tie in four seasons, and BBC Sport suggests springtime rugby at Thomond Park should be the aim."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "New Zealand: Richie Mo'unga may miss November Tests with calf injury",
          "body": "Jake White names first Fiji squad with uncapped newcomers."
