          "heading": "Shaun Edwards' Pumas deal rules out role under Steve Borthwick",
          "body": "Shaun Edwards' move to Argentina closes off any return to Steve Borthwick's England set-up, with Ruck reporting that he will not coach England at the 2027 World Cup. BBC Sport reported on 9 October that the former France defence coach has signed a deal with the Pumas running until the end of the 2027 World Cup in Australia. He and former Argentina hooker Mario Ledesma, who takes charge of the forwards, start work at the end of October, before November's Nations Championship matches against Ireland, Italy and France."
